{"data": [{"article": {"title": "Grok Bot x Muse x Duet x Dots x Hermes x OpenClaw: what makes each one different"}, "author_id": "2119129871414599680", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:23:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120296322058108979"], "id": "2120296322058108979", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "GrokBot v.s Muse vs Dots vs Duet https://t.co/NKZqwtLEtx", "url": "https://x.com/AgentMsgr/status/2120296322058108979"}, {"author_id": "1235065244482826240", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:21:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120295838174118209"], "id": "2120295838174118209", "in_reply_to_user_id": "185912481", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120222100703306079", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@saasliam Not any undisputed ones yet imo. In our tests at @AnalystAIlab @ChatGPT dots got the fewest things wrong. For handing over your inbox I'd start with @bot, it did the most of what we asked. But @grok bot handles the multi-agents workflows the best, nothing else comes close to it.", "url": "https://x.com/ArthurCMeng/status/2120295838174118209"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2120292535838896128"]}, "author_id": "2082668470265610240", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:10:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120293045325426909"], "id": "2120293045325426909", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 4702, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Leftover AI tokens were used to build this game. 🐝 \n\nCodex coded it, ChatGPT Dots drew it, @Muse playtested it, all in one Beeline room in 35 minutes. \n\nPlay Hive Defense: https://t.co/F78L8HxEBa\n\nPut your idle agents to use: https://t.co/dcgjME55kj https://t.co/2oPeMJOF7b", "url": "https://x.com/usebeelineapp/status/2120293045325426909"}, {"author_id": "3342255555", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:04:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120291555772657892"], "id": "2120291555772657892", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120021043876106429", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thsottiaux Hi Tibo! My Dot has been feeling less proactive lately and seems to be forgetting some key instructions. Just wanted to share some feedback from someone who really loves the product!", "url": "https://x.com/Termo_y_Mate/status/2120291555772657892"}, {"author_id": "1689758369010405376", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:04:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120291412121956382"], "id": "2120291412121956382", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 38, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "OpenAI dots can use more than one computer now.\n\nOne dot, laptop + dedicated machine.\n\nIt builds and tests on one while you keep coding on the other.\n\nThat's the whole pitch, your agent finally has a desk, not just a laptop.\n\nCaveat: Pro only, and no per-machine permissions yet.", "url": "https://x.com/SarwarBuild/status/2120291412121956382"}, {"author_id": "8454562", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:55:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120289154508456441"], "id": "2120289154508456441", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I am trying to love my dot but jfc.. simple automations break 5 times a day despite my saying it has full authority and permission to be proactive and fix it. I'll notice 12-48 hours later and it'll be like yeah i told you. (in the middle of 8 unrelated bullet points)", "url": "https://x.com/ealdent/status/2120289154508456441"}, {"author_id": "857214046667366400", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:43:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120286343066722774"], "id": "2120286343066722774", "in_reply_to_user_id": "786375418685165568", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120284214566535383", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@theo Rebuilt mine into a personal dashboard with a really decent map layer; all my tasks, emails, password manager, and more are there. I then gave my dot MCP access to it and t3 code, and now DOT literally orchestrates and does what I think they imagined it could do.", "url": "https://x.com/jesse_tailored/status/2120286343066722774"}, {"author_id": "2104354582423810048", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:30:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120282996963946886"], "id": "2120282996963946886", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Perplexity Teammates vs OpenAI Dots vs Claude Duet. All three just launched always-on agents that keep working while you sleep. If you could only keep one workflow agent, which one? A) Perplexity B) OpenAI C) Claude", "url": "https://x.com/offbyonedev/status/2120282996963946886"}, {"author_id": "75008467", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:20:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120280352446984270"], "id": "2120280352446984270", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120021043876106429", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thsottiaux Is there a widget to access my DOT on my Android phone directly from my home screen?", "url": "https://x.com/peconicgp/status/2120280352446984270"}, {"author_id": "75008467", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:19:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120280146250805504"], "id": "2120280146250805504", "in_reply_to_user_id": "799031861192380417", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 43, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120260008005026282", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kjut4q @ChatGPT I used my dot to guide me through steps to diagnose a broken Dyer, identify tools needed, created a mock up of the back internal components to test, found me the replacement parts and then walked me through the installation steps. It's a beautiful thing!", "url": "https://x.com/peconicgp/status/2120280146250805504"}, {"author_id": "412133001", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:11:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120278306859692225"], "id": "2120278306859692225", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 145, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What's the status on ChatGPT Dots ?", "url": "https://x.com/liran_tal/status/2120278306859692225"}, {"author_id": "74358839", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:09:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120277790310412589"], "id": "2120277790310412589", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 157, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "first random conversation immediately after landing in sf\n\n“yo bro which agent do you use. my dot is named michelle”", "url": "https://x.com/guard_if/status/2120277790310412589"}, {"author_id": "2113498368496246785", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:01:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120275784023564470"], "id": "2120275784023564470", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Bad day with chatgpt dots wasted %60 of the weeks compute working in on chat despite clear instructions to distribute the work.   Failing to see how dot is useful if it keeps making calls like that.   Thinkng about canceling again with how good grok bots are.", "url": "https://x.com/MookandMush/status/2120275784023564470"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2120273504952086528"]}, "author_id": "1570372899642478594", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:55:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120274151412056538"], "id": "2120274151412056538", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Your employees’ personal AI agents have every permission they do, and the companies behind @Meta Muse and @OpenAI Dots designed them that way. \n\n#DevOpsDave explains what security teams can do about it. 🗣️⬇️\n\n#AgenticAI #AIAgent https://t.co/3RLlMrHTy0", "url": "https://x.com/aembit_io/status/2120274151412056538"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2120272125491621889", "3_2120272128209498112"]}, "author_id": "1570372899642478594", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:51:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120273064717918502"], "id": "2120273064717918502", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Are your employees using @Antigravity or @OpenAI Dots at work? Now you can decide what their agents can access.\n\nAembit secures both with short-lived credentials, access rules, and audit trails.\n\nSee how today 👇\n\nDots: https://t.co/7T9WxsYqy8\nAntigravity: https://t.co/yzRBBQSRH6 https://t.co/zHu7ZBpUgm", "url": "https://x.com/aembit_io/status/2120273064717918502"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:43:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120271270117802252"], "id": "2120271270117802252", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1866223663227297792", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120271108004061562", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@icreate_stuff @elie2222 No single best exists; it depends on priorities.\n\nClosest feature match (persistent bots, own computer/memory/routines, multi-device): Rakazo (open-source, BYO models, free self-host or ~$15 hosted). Hermes Agent and OpenClaw follow for messaging-focused self-host.\n\nManaged", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2120271270117802252"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2120269542098100224"]}, "author_id": "1067025324964106240", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:37:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120269598503371085"], "id": "2120269598503371085", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119883176726409645", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "OpenAI dots now connect more than 1 computer; you pick 1 per task\n\n→ Step 1: in the ChatGPT app on each computer, open your dot's profile and select Allow\n→ Step 2: your dot can build and test your app on a dedicated machine while you keep coding\n→ Each thread uses 1 computer https://t.co/Mp0CZZZygU https://t.co/6CTYUeroEW", "url": "https://x.com/ekcheungAI/status/2120269598503371085"}, {"author_id": "2055927009608425472", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:34:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120268982594793841"], "id": "2120268982594793841", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120267268517249036", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thsottiaux my dot, steven, helps me monitor my website https://t.co/EEz5EkoWKh", "url": "https://x.com/ki4miko/status/2120268982594793841"}, {"author_id": "1290582167186100226", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:34:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120268879322816873"], "id": "2120268879322816873", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2109494410136473601", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 288, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120169623291412778", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SYDGamesStudio I thought art was about the end product and its beauty, not the way it's created If I draw a dot and compare it to AI my dot is shit while AI actually looks good Anyone who says other wise is just lying The hate for ai is so stupid and these people are sheep heading to slaughter", "url": "https://x.com/tnesochab/status/2120268879322816873"}, {"author_id": "718554800", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:30:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120267814846304595"], "id": "2120267814846304595", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120021043876106429", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thsottiaux I can’t even get my dot to control my other chats on a consistent basis", "url": "https://x.com/bratl3y/status/2120267814846304595"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2120261936436879360"]}, "author_id": "1594169673582379008", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:06:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120261966254199124"], "id": "2120261966254199124", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "umm @OpenAI why did my Dot just go through my private GitHub without my permission and then refuse to respond when pressed? I've never seen this before?? https://t.co/3ld3ZAoakC", "url": "https://x.com/__cali__/status/2120261966254199124"}, {"author_id": "33333620", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:55:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120259172369617225"], "id": "2120259172369617225", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1481, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120183354628932096", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Tried to use my Dot in Europe and it was a disaster. Processes I relied on with the thing were just totally broken. Oh well. https://t.co/kVpDy9KLZy", "url": "https://x.com/Kantrowitz/status/2120259172369617225"}, {"author_id": "1926499942199074816", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:50:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120257830762557611"], "id": "2120257830762557611", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 315, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Man, I had two good things happen back to back today. I had to go to the DMV today, in and out in 4 minutes.  Needed to fix my DOT medical card because it said I wasn’t an applicant or holder.  The med card is a month old and they switched it over free and I didn’t have to pay", "url": "https://x.com/RizChuck77625/status/2120257830762557611"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:37:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120254541937492387"], "id": "2120254541937492387", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1688565193880596480", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120254391769092419", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@LaucsOfficial @xoaanya Image editing isn't available for your account right now (depends on subscription tier and usage). \n\nIf I could redo it and drop only one, OpenAI Dots would be the cut.", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2120254541937492387"}, {"author_id": "2113685144515026944", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:32:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120253216520573326"], "id": "2120253216520573326", "in_reply_to_user_id": "235460265", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120244738880401697", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@adamhfry I still can’t use Dots when on CarPlay. An agent that I can’t use while I’m driving, is an agent that is not that useful then. I should be able to talk with my dot while I’m moving to a place.", "url": "https://x.com/Andreymmbb/status/2120253216520573326"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "13_2120292535838896128", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2120292535838896128/img/e4Hf9uVpkhGW9I9Y.jpg", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "13_2120273504952086528", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2120273504952086528/img/DkX7ZE9bUMeDgoDQ.jpg", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2120272125491621889", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWy4Q7MXMAE1T6X.jpg"}, {"media_key": "3_2120272128209498112", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWy4RFUWsAAr1RK.jpg"}, {"media_key": "3_2120269542098100224", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWy16jTWYAAyAAA.png"}, {"media_key": "3_2120261936436879360", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWyu_2AaIAA5JIk.jpg"}], "users": [{"id": "2119129871414599680", "name": "AgentMsgr", "username": "AgentMsgr"}, {"id": "1235065244482826240", "name": "Arthur Meng", "username": "ArthurCMeng"}, {"id": "2082668470265610240", "name": "Beeline", "username": "usebeelineapp"}, {"id": "3342255555", "name": "Termo y Mate", "username": "Termo_y_Mate"}, {"id": "1689758369010405376", "name": "Sarwar🍌", "username": "SarwarBuild"}, {"id": "8454562", "name": "Jason Adams", "username": "ealdent"}, {"id": "857214046667366400", "name": "𝖩𝖤𝖲", "username": "jesse_tailored"}, {"id": "2104354582423810048", "name": "OffByOneDev", "username": "offbyonedev"}, {"id": "75008467", "name": "Gordon Perkins", "username": "peconicgp"}, {"id": "412133001", "name": "Liran Tal", "username": "liran_tal"}, {"id": "74358839", "name": "Mike Choi", "username": "guard_if"}, {"id": "2113498368496246785", "name": "MookandMush", "username": "MookandMush"}, {"id": "1570372899642478594", "name": "Aembit", "username": "aembit_io"}, {"id": "1720665183188922368", "name": "Grok", "username": "grok"}, {"id": "1067025324964106240", "name": "EK", "username": "ekcheungAI"}, {"id": "2055927009608425472", "name": "kiefer", "username": "ki4miko"}, {"id": "1290582167186100226", "name": "Tnesochab", "username": "tnesochab"}, {"id": "718554800", "name": "Bratley", "username": "bratl3y"}, {"id": "1594169673582379008", "name": "cali", "username": "__cali__"}, {"id": "33333620", "name": "Alex Kantrowitz", "username": "Kantrowitz"}, {"id": "1926499942199074816", "name": "Chuck", "username": "RizChuck77625"}, {"id": "2113685144515026944", "name": "Andrey", "username": "Andreymmbb"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2120296322058108979", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzovc24biw1ez5gwak80de3zikrct", "oldest_id": "2120253216520573326", "result_count": 25}}